  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday Night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1101 AM CDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nThe ridge continues its hold on the southeastern United States into \nthe weekend, where temperatures somehow manage to get even hotter. \nHighs on the weekend have a real chance of reaching 100 degrees in \nsome areas on the Highland Rim. With the heat advisory in effect for \nthe area, and the extreme heat risk, precautions need to be made for \noutdoor activities. Make sure you are staying hydrated and taking \nfrequent breaks in the shade or A/C if you still plan to be outside \nthis weekend. \n\nOnce we start a new work week, A low pressure system in Canada will \nbegin to exert pressure on our ridge, and we are squeezed right in \nthe middle. As the low dips further south, some passing shortwaves \nwill bring rain chances starting Monday night. While chances are low \n(20 - 30%), a weak cold front will shift our winds to be from the \nnorth and lower highs on Tuesday to the low 90s. Unfortunately, it \nis August, so we will bounce right back to the mid 90s into the \nmiddle of the week.",
